<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_volume" target="china_west_rivalry::export_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid increases in arms transfers and discovery of Western-origin or dual-use components in fielded Russian systems prompt Western governments to widen and tighten export controls on dual‑use tech and components, including measures that extend to suppliers and end‑users linked to China.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">china_west_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_volume" target="global_energy_shock::refined_fuel_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Larger flows of weapons and associated logistics increase military consumption of diesel/jet fuel and create congestion at ports and logistics hubs, tightening local commercial refined‑fuel availability and pushing wholesale/retail prices higher.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_volume" target="monetary_policy_shock::bank_funding_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Surges in arms transfers elevate cross‑border payments through sanctioned or opaque channels and concentrate counterparty exposure in certain banks, raising correspondent‑bank risk and liquidity hoarding which increases wholesale funding stress.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">monetary_policy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_volume" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::accidental_engagement_ri" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased global arms flows linked to the Russia–Ukraine war expand the number and heterogeneity of missile, drone, and electronic systems in regional inventories, raising the probability of misfires, misidentification, and technical failures that cause accidental engagements in the Gulf theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
