  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Conflict‑driven disruptions to energy supplies push up domestic and imported energy prices, producing near‑term headline inflationary impulses that compel monetary authorities to raise policy rates to anchor inflation expectations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">monetary_policy_shock</data>
</edge>
