  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising perceived maritime transport risk increases insurance and logistics costs and projected delivery risk for hardware‑heavy AI projects, prompting investors and lenders to pull or reprice capital for those ventures and thereby reducing funding flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">china_west_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_gulf_conflict::shipping_risk_perception" target="global_energy_shock::crude_oil_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in commercial and insurer perceptions of maritime risk raises freight and insurance premia and prompts market participants to add a supply-risk premium to crude futures, lifting crude prices independent of immediate physical incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
