<edge source="us_iran_gulf_conflict::escalation_momentum" target="china_west_rivalry::export_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained escalation in the Gulf prompts Western governments to rapidly expand and tighten export controls on dual‑use technologies and equipment to deny potential combatants or proxies sensitive capabilities, increasing overall export restriction intensity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">china_west_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_gulf_conflict::escalation_momentum" target="global_energy_shock::upstream_prod_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained escalation drives operators and host authorities to curtail production, evacuate personnel, delay maintenance and investment, and order shut‑ins in exposed fields, reducing upstream output volumes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_gulf_conflict::escalation_momentum" target="monetary_policy_shock::policy_interest_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained escalation drives energy and commodity price spikes and exchange‑rate pressure in exposed economies, producing higher headline inflation and capital outflow risks that prompt monetary authorities to raise policy rates to defend price stability and the currency.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">monetary_policy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_gulf_conflict::escalation_momentum" target="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_incentives" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Growing escalation momentum in the Gulf creates windows where US and allied attention and political will are constrained, which Russia can interpret as lowered risk of coordinated Western escalation and thus raises its incentives to escalate in Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
