<edge source="china_west_rivalry::ai_model_deployment_rate" target="global_energy_shock::energy_price_inflation" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">1</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Accelerated deployment of large AI models increases datacenter electricity demand in constrained grids, raising wholesale power costs and contributing to the energy component of consumer price inflation.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_west_rivalry::ai_model_deployment_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_conflict_intensi" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Faster deployment of trained AI models into operational ISR, targeting and autonomous systems raises strike tempo and precision (and enables more remote/automated kinetic effects), increasing the overall intensity of kinetic operations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_west_rivalry::ai_model_deployment_rate" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::accidental_engagement_ri" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid rollout of unvetted or poorly integrated AI for maritime identification, threat scoring, or automated responses increases misclassification and automated escalation triggers, raising the instantaneous risk of unintended kinetic exchanges.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
