<edge source="china_west_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="monetary_policy_shock::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls immediately block transactions, approvals and deal closings and prompt multinationals and funds to pause or cancel cross‑border investments and transfers into affected tech sectors, shrinking net cross‑border capital flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">monetary_policy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_west_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="monetary_policy_shock::bank_funding_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sudden, broad export restrictions create payment frictions, correspondent‑banking disruptions and collateral repricing for banks with exposed clients, increasing short‑term funding premia and liquidity stress.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">monetary_policy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_west_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stricter export controls on advanced chips and dual‑use tech to China and third‑party intermediaries reduce China’s ability to re‑export or broker components to Russia, lowering the net flow of sophisticated weapon components into the conflict.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_west_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::diplomatic_engagement_in" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stricter export controls on dual‑use tech increase incentives for China to deepen security ties and transfers with Iran (and for regional states to seek reassurance), prompting intensified US and third‑party diplomatic activity to manage or roll back transfers and tensions.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
