<edge source="global_energy_shock::shipping_security_risk" target="china_west_rivalry::chip_supply_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising maritime security incidents (attacks, interdictions, or blockades) immediately raise insurance and rerouting costs, delay shipments of wafers, tools and finished chips and force temporary idling or underfeeding of fabs, reducing effective chip supply capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">china_west_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::shipping_security_risk" target="monetary_policy_shock::bank_funding_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Elevated maritime security risk disrupts trade flows and trade finance lines, raises counterparty and collateral risk for banks active in commodity and shipping finance, and leads to higher wholesale funding costs and roll‑over difficulty.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">monetary_policy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::shipping_security_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_disruption_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher maritime security incidents (attacks, seizures, blockades) directly interrupt tanker movements and pipeline feeder logistics, causing measurable disruptions to energy supply chains and delivery timetables into Europe and adjacent markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::shipping_security_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased risk to sea transport raises insurance, rerouting and delay costs for bulk shipments (including large munitions and heavy equipment), reducing the feasible volume and timeliness of arms deliveries into the theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::shipping_security_risk" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::kinetic_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in maritime security risk reflects and incentivizes more hostile patrols, interdictions and strikes by state and proxy actors against shipping, directly raising the frequency and intensity of kinetic attacks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::shipping_security_risk" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::accidental_engagement_ri" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher security risk drives denser armed escorts, more frequent close-quarter maneuvers and elevated rules-of-engagement, which raise the instantaneous probability of misidentification or technical errors producing accidental kinetic exchanges.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
