<edge source="global_energy_shock::energy_price_inflation" target="china_west_rivalry::capital_funding_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in the energy component of inflation pressures central banks toward tighter policy and raises operating costs for compute‑intensive AI firms, which reduces investor risk appetite and the rate of new capital deployment into AI projects across China and the West.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">china_west_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::energy_price_inflation" target="monetary_policy_shock::policy_interest_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A material rise in the energy component of inflation pushes headline and near‑term inflation expectations higher, prompting monetary authorities to raise policy rates to re-anchor expectations and tighten financial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">monetary_policy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::energy_price_inflation" target="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_cohesion_leve" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A rising energy component of consumer inflation intensifies domestic economic and political pressure on coalition governments to prioritize relief and lower-energy-dependence policies, weakening unity and coordinated diplomatic pressure on Russia.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::energy_price_inflation" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::diplomatic_engagement_in" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in the energy component of inflation creates immediate domestic economic pressure that prompts the U.S. and partners to intensify diplomatic activity to secure Gulf energy flows and coordinate mitigation measures.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
