<edge source="monetary_policy_shock::sovereign_spread_level" target="china_west_rivalry::chip_supply_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Widening sovereign spreads raise government financing costs and reduce fiscal space for subsidies and guarantees that underpin state‑backed semiconductor capacity expansions, causing postponement or cancellation of planned fabs and reducing capacity growth.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_policy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">china_west_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_policy_shock::sovereign_spread_level" target="global_energy_shock::upstream_prod_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher sovereign spreads in oil‑exporting jurisdictions raise sovereign and state‑owned enterprise borrowing costs and constrain budgeted upstream capex and maintenance, leading to lower production rates as projects are delayed or curtailed.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_policy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_policy_shock::sovereign_spread_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_cohesion_leve" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Widening sovereign spreads among coalition states increases domestic economic and political pressure to prioritize fiscal stabilization, making governments more reluctant to sustain costly coordinated sanctions, financial support, or unified diplomatic stances and thereby reducing diplomatic cohesion.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_policy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_policy_shock::sovereign_spread_level" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::diplomatic_engagement_in" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Widening sovereign spreads raise debt‑service and rollover costs, forcing regional governments and potential mediators to reallocate scarce fiscal and political capital away from active mediation and diplomatic outreach in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_policy_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
